{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>To the priest who shall be in those days.</b> Even though he may not be great in wisdom, you must not refrain from speaking to him with honor, saying ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ — even though this would not be said to anyone other than men of the Name, such as kings and prophets. Nevertheless, since you bring him the first fruits as one bringing a gift to the Most High, who is the owner of the land, it is fitting that you speak to him in this manner, with honor." "<b>I have declared today.</b> I have made known to all through these actions of mine, as in כִּי הִגַּדְתָּ הַיּוֹם כִּי אַיִן לְךָ שָׂרִים וַעֲבָדִים (II Samuel 19:7)." "<b>That I have come to the land.</b> That I have come from another land to this land." "<b>Which HaShem swore to our fathers to give us.</b> As it says: וְנָתַתִּי לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ וְכוּ׳ (ibid.). Therefore, I the ger who have come to the land as a settler by the power of His gift — I have brought the first fruits that are fitting to give to the owner of land by way of gift or sharecropping."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Reading זוּלָתִי as 'other than me' (i.e., 'other than this person'); the referent is the priest addressed, understood as 'this one.'", 3 "Citation marked שם refers back to II Samuel 19:7, but the quoted verse (וְנָתַתִּי לְךָ...) is from Genesis, likely Genesis 17:8; Sforno's שם may refer to a different prior source or there is a textual issue."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:16.384903887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}